        <p class="profile-detail-region">Battle · Central &amp; East Asia</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Shanghai</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">13 August to 26 November 1937, in three stages: 13 to 22 August, 23 August to 26 October, and 27 October to the end of November</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanghai">Shanghai</a> and its surroundings: the city's districts, the creek country to the north, the coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze</a> delta and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hangzhou">Hangzhou</a> Bay, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chiang-kai-shek">Chiang Kai-shek</a>, with commanders including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhang-zhizhong">Zhang Zhizhong</a> and Chen Cheng; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a>, with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanghai">Shanghai</a> Expeditionary Army under Iwane Matsui. The battle eventually involved around one million troops. In early October the Japanese had more than 200,000 troops in the region against over 700,000 Chinese deployed across a wide front.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Japanese captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanghai">Shanghai</a> after more than three months of fighting on land, in the air and at sea. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> lost a significant portion of its best troops and no foreign power intervened.</span></div>
